Given these tables:

CREATE TABLE customers (id INTEGER, name TEXT, country TEXT);
INSERT INTO customers VALUES (1,'Ada','DE'),(2,'Bo','SE'),(3,'Cy','DE'),(4,'Di','FR'),(5,'Ed','SE'),(6,'Fi','FR');
CREATE TABLE orders (id INTEGER, customer_id INTEGER, amount REAL, status TEXT);
INSERT INTO orders VALUES (1,1,120,'paid'),(2,1,80,'refunded'),(3,2,60,'paid'),(4,3,45,'paid'),
(5,4,200,'paid'),(6,5,30,'paid'),(7,5,55,'paid'),(8,2,40,'pending'),(9,3,70,'paid'),(10,4,15,'refunded'),
(11,3,NULL,'paid');

What does this query return (SQLite)?

SELECT c.name, COUNT(o.id) AS orders, COUNT(o.amount) AS priced, COALESCE(SUM(CASE WHEN o.status = 'paid' THEN o.amount END), 0) AS paid FROM customers c LEFT JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.id GROUP BY c.id ORDER BY paid DESC, c.name

Answer as a JSON array of rows, each [name, orders, priced, paid], in the query's order. Output only the JSON: no prose, no code fences.
